iCARE / iHOPE  (17-section format, transcripts, expert gold notes)
  No licence file, and no statement of terms in the README -- verified
  2026-08-24. The transcripts and gold notes are fetched from ai4mhx/TheraFuse,
  which displays an MIT badge but ships no LICENSE file; the corpus it
  redistributes was collected elsewhere, so that badge is not a licence for the
  data. This repository therefore reproduces neither the instructions nor the
  notes, with one stated exception: the methods page quotes one section of one
  iHOPE note, in the clinician's wording and one model's, as the worked example
  that shows word overlap is not quality. Everything else is section field
  names, and only for display.
  https://github.com/proadhikary/iCARE
  https://github.com/ai4mhx/TheraFuse
  Adhikary, Prottay Kumar; Singh, S.; Singh, S.; Sharma, P.; Soni, P.;
  Choudhary, R.; Saxena, C.; Chauhan, P.; Gupta, Swati Kedia; Deb, K. S.;
  Singh, S. M.; Chakraborty, Tanmoy. "Clinically Grounded AI-Scribing in
  Psychotherapy: Benchmarking LLMs Against Expert Documentation in the iCARE
  Framework." medRxiv 2025.06.25.25330252 (v2, 2026-08-19). CC-BY.

  Because no licence is attached to the data, this repository never vendors,
  mirrors or republishes it. See docs/datasets.md.
